ll  he would have to come in at  1am what it was a whole other two hours  to get it off at the end of the day  here's hoping jaime could sleep through  that or he'd never sleep at all his day  started at 3am to be ready for 10 am he  and the makeup artists would all chill  and listen to heavy rock music while the  prosthetics were being applied and jaime  would use the tone to get into character  otherwise he'd read a book and on rare  occasions sip on coffee for me you know  i'm a small cog in a very very big wheel  number eight paint me like one of your  vectors barry the concept art was great  but translating that to the real thing  was a challenge to find the right colors  they looked at different sea life and  human bruises they had an overwhelming  number of colors to choose from and  reeling it in was hard we had to really  hone it in to only a few colors they  settled on one makeup palette from  premiere products with 10 different  colors and that was it number nine gotta  stay sticky jamie was just covered in  lube and a wet looking gel to give vecna  a glossy look every day it would be four  dudes who would have about 15 minutes to  coat him with it and people would come  up and try and shake his hand and just  regret it immediately we can only wonder  how jaime feels under there he was given  dentures and contact lenses to finish it  off we really put him through the mill  there wasn't anything else we could get  on jamie number 10 got your nose jaime  not every part of vechna could be  practical unfortunately this isn't  2004's spider-man with doc ock this is  more like 2021's doc ock just let cgi  handle the inhuman stuff the living  vines were added in post none of that  was there so that was kind of just like  strain my arms and my neck to make it  look like there was something wrapped  around them that goes for not only  vacna's vines but all the vines our  heroes weren't jumping over anything  they were just jumping from tape mark to  tape mark on t